course: dictionary
lesson: 9996
title: Teeny words, big hiding places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Teeny is an informal word that means very small or tiny. Stories and baby talk use it to make things sound sweet: a teeny kitten, a teeny spider. Look at the words around it to be sure of its meaning.
explain: Small words can also hide big things. «I lost by a teeny bit» sounds like a near miss, but the real numbers may be 3 votes to 27. The word teeny makes the loss sound much smaller than it was.
explain: When you read, ask two questions. Does this word make something sound smaller than it really is? What are the real numbers or facts? Then compare the words with the facts before you decide what is true.
fact: Teeny means very small or tiny.
fact: Teeny is informal, so it belongs in chatty talk and stories, not in formal writing.
fact: Teeny-weeny and teeny-tiny mean extremely small, and they are childish words.
fact: «A teeny problem» can hide a big one, because a speaker may play down how serious something is.
fact: Wee means small in Scotland and Ireland, and tiny and itsy-bitsy are close in meaning to teeny.
exercise: «There is a teeny spider on the window.» What does teeny mean here? | Very sticky | Very loud | *Very small | Very old
exercise: Maya says, «I lost by a teeny bit», but the votes were 3 to 27. Why might her words be misleading? | Teeny means the votes were very close | *Teeny hides how big the loss really was | Teeny makes a big loss sound small | Teeny means she won the vote
exercise: Which word is the closest match for teeny? | Curt | Enormous | *Tiny | Ancient
test: «The teeny problem was really a huge mess.» What does this sentence show? | *A small word can hide a big problem | The mess was tiny | Problems never matter | Teeny always means big
test: In Scotland and Ireland, what does «wee» mean? | *Small | Wet | Very old | Angry
exam: «Teeny-weeny» means what? | Very slow | Very loud | *Extremely small | Very large
